From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:58:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 79/79] A library or package compiles with the global-dynamic
 TLS model

With section threadvars (Linux x86_64, i386 and arm when the compiler is
built with -dtls_threadvars), the options pass picks the TLS model before
the first module is parsed: global-dynamic with -Cg, otherwise
local-exec. A library or package without -Cg therefore accessed its
threadvars with local-exec code, which is only valid in the executable:

- x86_64-linux turns on PIC when the parser reaches `library`, after
  that choice. Each threadvar access took the address RIP-relative and
  added a %fs override, and the library crashed on its first threadvar
  access:

      lea  Counter(%rip),%rdx
      addl $1,%fs:(%rdx)

- i386-linux libraries are not PIC by default. dlopen refused them:
  "cannot allocate memory in static TLS block".

Use global-dynamic for a library or package, and for the units a library
compiles, whenever the local-exec model was chosen. An explicit
-CVlocal-exec cannot be told apart and is switched too, which a shared
object needs anyway. Programs keep local-exec; -Cg builds are unchanged.
---
 compiler/pmodules.pas | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/pmodules.pas b/compiler/pmodules.pas
index 89bec8e2..d81dec6e 100644
--- a/compiler/pmodules.pas
+++ b/compiler/pmodules.pas
@@ -2002,6 +2002,10 @@ type
 
          if tf_library_needs_pic in target_info.flags then
            include(current_settings.moduleswitches,cs_create_pic);
+         { a shared object cannot use the local-exec TLS model }
+         if (tf_section_threadvars in target_info.flags) and
+            (current_settings.tlsmodel=tlsm_local_exec) then
+           current_settings.tlsmodel:=tlsm_global_dynamic;
 
          { setup things using the switches, do this before the semicolon, because after the semicolon has been
            read, all following directives are parsed as well }
@@ -2846,6 +2850,14 @@ type
            { also set create_pic for all unit compilation }
            include(init_settings.moduleswitches,cs_create_pic);
          end;
+        { a shared object cannot use the local-exec TLS model, neither in its own code nor in the units it compiles }
+        if tf_section_threadvars in target_info.flags then
+          begin
+            if current_settings.tlsmodel=tlsm_local_exec then
+              current_settings.tlsmodel:=tlsm_global_dynamic;
+            if init_settings.tlsmodel=tlsm_local_exec then
+              init_settings.tlsmodel:=tlsm_global_dynamic;
+          end;
 
         { setup things using the switches, do this before the semicolon, because after the semicolon has been
          read, all following directives are parsed as well }
